==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ˈfɪs.tɪ.kʌfs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-fisticuffs.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# A [[derivative]] of [[boxing]] in which two [[opponent]]s tie either their right or left [[wrist]]s together and [[box]] with their free hands.
# {{informal}} An [[impromptu]] fight with the fists, usually between two people.

====Quotations====
*'''2007''', [[w:The Argus (Brighton)|The Argus]], "[http://www.theargus.co.uk/display.var.1562598.0.brothers_guilty_of_attacking_barman_in_pub.php Brothers guilty of attacking barman in pub],"
*:He added: "You are both far too old to indulge in this sort of pub '''fisticuffs'''."

